<section class="richardson-tool" data-richardson-tool>
	<div class="tool-panel hero-panel">
		<p class="eyebrow">Finite element verification</p>
		<h2>Richardson extrapolation for mesh convergence studies</h2>
		<p>
			Enter three systematically refined meshes, from coarsest to finest, to estimate the continuum value and the 95%
			confidence interval using the Grid Convergence Index method.
		</p>
		<p class="hero-note">
			Use consistent units for mesh edge length and result value. The factor of safety is fixed at <strong>1.25</strong>,
			which matches the previous tool.
		</p>
	</div>

	<form class="tool-panel input-panel" data-form novalidate>
		<div class="section-heading">
			<div>
				<h3>Input data</h3>
				<p>Mesh sizes must decrease each row. Result values can be any consistent scalar quantity from your analysis.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="button-row">
				<button type="button" class="ghost-button" data-action="sample">Load sample data</button>
				<button type="submit">Calculate extrapolation</button>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="table-wrap">
			<table class="mesh-table">
				<thead>
					<tr>
						<th scope="col">Mesh level</th>
						<th scope="col">Element edge length</th>
						<th scope="col">Result value</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Coarsest mesh</th>
						<td>
							<label class="sr-only" for="mesh-size-1">Coarsest mesh element edge length</label>
							<input id="mesh-size-1" data-key="meshSize1" inputmode="decimal" step="any" type="number" value="2" />
						</td>
						<td>
							<label class="sr-only" for="result-value-1">Coarsest mesh result value</label>
							<input id="result-value-1" data-key="resultValue1" inputmode="decimal" step="any" type="number" value="200" />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Medium mesh</th>
						<td>
							<label class="sr-only" for="mesh-size-2">Medium mesh element edge length</label>
							<input id="mesh-size-2" data-key="meshSize2" inputmode="decimal" step="any" type="number" value="1" />
						</td>
						<td>
							<label class="sr-only" for="result-value-2">Medium mesh result value</label>
							<input id="result-value-2" data-key="resultValue2" inputmode="decimal" step="any" type="number" value="210" />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Finest mesh</th>
						<td>
							<label class="sr-only" for="mesh-size-3">Finest mesh element edge length</label>
							<input id="mesh-size-3" data-key="meshSize3" inputmode="decimal" step="any" type="number" value="0.5" />
						</td>
						<td>
							<label class="sr-only" for="result-value-3">Finest mesh result value</label>
							<input id="result-value-3" data-key="resultValue3" inputmode="decimal" step="any" type="number" value="215" />
						</td>
					</tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>

		<p class="status-message" data-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
	</form>

	<div class="results-grid">
		<section class="tool-panel output-panel">
			<div class="section-heading">
				<div>
					<h3>Output data</h3>
					<p>The extrapolated result is the estimated continuum value based on your finest three meshes.</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<dl class="metric-grid">
				<div class="metric-card">
					<dt>Estimated exact value</dt>
					<dd data-field="extrapolatedValue">--</dd>
				</div>
				<div class="metric-card">
					<dt>95% lower bound</dt>
					<dd data-field="lowerBound">--</dd>
				</div>
				<div class="metric-card">
					<dt>95% upper bound</dt>
					<dd data-field="upperBound">--</dd>
				</div>
				<div class="metric-card">
					<dt>Order of convergence</dt>
					<dd data-field="orderOfConvergence">--</dd>
				</div>
				<div class="metric-card">
					<dt>Convergence check</dt>
					<dd data-field="convergenceCheck">--</dd>
				</div>
				<div class="metric-card">
					<dt>Fine-grid GCI</dt>
					<dd data-field="gci23">--</dd>
				</div>
				<div class="metric-card">
					<dt>Refinement ratios</dt>
					<dd data-field="ratios">--</dd>
				</div>
				<div class="metric-card">
					<dt>Iterations</dt>
					<dd data-field="iterations">--</dd>
				</div>
			</dl>

			<div class="warnings-panel">
				<h4>Checks</h4>
				<ul class="warning-list" data-warnings>
					<li>No warnings yet.</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="tool-panel chart-panel">
			<div class="section-heading">
				<div>
					<h3>Grid convergence plot</h3>
					<p>The chart shows the three mesh results and the continuum estimate at zero mesh size.</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="chart-frame">
				<svg data-chart viewBox="0 0 720 360" role="img" aria-label="Grid convergence plot"></svg>
				<p class="chart-empty" data-chart-empty>Valid results will appear here after calculation.</p>
			</div>
			<p class="chart-caption" data-chart-caption>Confidence bounds are shown around the extrapolated exact value.</p>
		</section>
	</div>

	<section class="tool-panel notes-panel">
		<div class="section-heading">
			<div>
				<h3>Interpretation notes</h3>
				<p>These checks help you decide whether the mesh sequence is good enough for a credible continuum estimate.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
		<ul class="notes-list">
			<li>Keep the mesh sizes in descending order from coarse to fine.</li>
			<li>Refinement ratios below 1.3 are often too narrow for a stable extrapolation.</li>
			<li>A convergence check close to 1.0 suggests the solution is approaching the asymptotic range.</li>
			<li>Oscillatory convergence means the result changes sign between refinements and deserves extra scrutiny.</li>
		</ul>
		<p class="references">
			References:
			<a href="https://www.grc.nasa.gov/www/wind/valid/tutorial/spatconv.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NASA spatial convergence guide</a>
			and
			<a href="https://www.dynamore.de/de/download/papers/forum08/dokumente/I-I-03.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DYNAmore Richardson extrapolation paper</a>.
		</p>
	</section>
</section>

<style>
